      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Secret Management**\n\nOkay, I'm setting the stage for `fetch_db_secret.py`. It's essential to define the external secret provider. I've decided to use AWS Secrets Manager. Now I need to figure out the code's identifiable elements for this AWS service.\n\n\n**Identifying Key Elements**\n\nI've homed in on the specifics for `fetch_db_secret.py`, nailing down AWS Secrets Manager as the provider. Key identifiable components will be the `boto3` library for AWS, the `aws_secret_manager` client, the `get_secret_value` API call, and the `SecretString` from the response. I'm ready to move into writing the file.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820711221,
          "start": 1789820708463
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9a0a66f001B9M1MkArDxjx3H",
